Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> On 01.07.2014 23:05, Patric Mueller wrote:
>> Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
>>> [ fast update of junethack server from NAO data ]
>> 
>> Junethack uses the xlogfile from NAO. This file is updated by the NAO
>> server the moment your game has finished.
>
> Does it use that global huge xlogfile which on NAO is ~1GB ?
> For performance consideration I suppose it does a delta-download then?

Yes and yes. When the junethack server polls for the first time, it
only asks the NAO server how large the file is and afterwards it only
ask for the byte range that it hasn't seen yet.

This is standard HTTP 1.1 functionality and usually well supported on
web servers.

Downloading the whole xlogfile just to throw it away would be
time and bandwidth consuming.

BTW, the sizes of the xlogfiles on the different public servers are
quite big. NAO has ~910 MB, un.nethack.nu ~180 MB, and sporkhack.com
has ~4 MB. The other public server participating in Junethack have
xlogfiles at about 1 MB or smaller.

